course: dictionary
lesson: 15160
title: One word, many meanings: scoring
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word «scoring» is a good example: it can be about games, about rules, about cutting card, or about music.
explain: Look for the clue words around it. Next to a ball, a goal or a team, «scoring» means getting points. Next to a rule about how many points a basket is worth, it means how points are counted.
explain: Ask yourself: what is being done here? If someone is cutting light lines in card so it folds neatly, that is a craft. If someone is writing the tunes for a film, that is music. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: Scoring means getting points or goals in a game.
fact: Scoring also means the rule for how points are counted, such as «two points for each basket».
fact: Scoring means cutting light lines into card or a surface so it folds or breaks neatly.
fact: Scoring means writing music for a film or band.
fact: The words around «scoring» show you which meaning is right, so always read the whole sentence.
exercise: «Scoring the winning goal, Sam was cheered by the whole team.» What does scoring mean here? | Writing music for a film | *Getting goals in a game | Counting marks in a test | Cutting lines in card
exercise: «Before folding the card, scoring a line along the fold makes it crease neatly.» What does scoring mean here? | *Cutting a light line so the card folds neatly | Getting points in a game | Adding up the points for each basket | Writing music for a film
exercise: «The scoring is two points for each basket.» What does scoring mean here? | *The rule for how points are counted | Getting goals in a game | Writing a tune for a band | Cutting paper into shapes
test: «The composer is scoring the music for the new film.» What does scoring mean here? | Cutting lines in card | *Writing music for a film | Counting the points in a test | Getting points in a game
test: Maya says scoring only ever means goals. Is she right? | No, scoring means making a sandwich | *No, scoring can also mean the rule for counting points | Yes, scoring means reading very fast | Yes, scoring only ever means goals
exam: In «The scoring guide tells the teachers how many marks each answer gets», what does scoring mean? | Cutting lines in card | Writing music for a band | Getting goals in a game | *The rule for how points or marks are counted
